IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): THE NOUNS.
-- Layer 1, module 1. Types and one shim only; no rule of the Order is stated here.
-- Every other uro- module imports this one.
--
-- Method. The Order is an amending instrument: it states new figures for sums that sit in other
-- instruments (the Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, the Income Support Regulations, the Housing Benefit
-- Regulations and so on), none of which is among the inputs. So:
--   * a figure the Order states (a substituted sum, a sum it says remains unchanged, a figure in one of
--     its 13 Schedules) is a VALUE, cited with @ref and src: locators;
--   * a sum the Order says is "increased by 3.8 per cent" is a function of the sum the parent instrument
--     now carries; that sum is a plain input, marked "-- out of text:";
--   * a category the Order's tables key on but leave to a parent instrument ("satisfies the condition in
--     paragraph 11(1)(a)") is a plain input named for the fact.
-- Money is in pounds as a NUMBER. Art 11 states pence; it is carried in pence and says so.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk (version 2026-03-05), not the official text.

-- The stable prelude has no YMD (writing-l4-rules/references/dialects.md, probe 05): a local shim,
-- day-first Date underneath. Defined once, here; every other module gets it by importing this one.
YMD y m d MEANS Date d m y

-- A sum the Order replaces ("for 118.75 substitute 123.25"), or restates unchanged ("remains unchanged",
-- both fields equal). Both figures are stated by the Order itself, so both are values.
DECLARE `a sum and its replacement` HAS
    `the sum before the Order` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum after the Order` IS A NUMBER

-- "under pensionable age" and "over pensionable age" (Sch 1 Part IV item 1A) are the only positions the
-- text names. A beneficiary exactly AT pensionable age is in neither on the words used (see NOTES.md, fork F-04).
DECLARE `a position relative to pensionable age` IS ONE OF
    `under pensionable age`
    `at pensionable age`
    `over pensionable age`

-- The fifteen places in a non-dependant deductions provision where the Order changes a sum. The six
-- provisions (arts 20(6), 23(3), 24(3), 26(7), 29(4), 30(7)) have exactly the same fifteen sub-paragraphs.
-- The Order says only "non-dependant deductions" of each: what each sum is a deduction FOR is in the
-- parent instrument, so a sub-paragraph reference is the only key the Order gives.
DECLARE `a sub-paragraph of a non-dependant deduction provision` IS ONE OF
    `sub-paragraph (1)(a)`
    `sub-paragraph (1)(b)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(a)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(b)(i)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(b)(ii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(b)(iii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(c)(i)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(c)(ii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(c)(iii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(d)(i)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(d)(ii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(d)(iii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(e)(i)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(e)(ii)`
    `sub-paragraph (2)(e)(iii)`
